<title>USA: LPC-Nash Finch taps banks for $500 mln bank loan.</title>
<headline>LPC-Nash Finch taps banks for $500 mln bank loan.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Oct 11 (LPC) - Bank of Montreal's Harris Bank, Bank of Montreal and PNC Bank are leading a $500 million bank loan backing Nash Finch Co's acquisition of Super Food Services, according to a Securities and Exchange Commission filing.</p>
<p>Pricing on the senior unsecured, five-year revolver ranges from 20 to 70 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR), plus a 10- to 30-basis-point annual fee, based on debt ratings, according to the filing.</p>
<p>Harris Bank has committed $30 million, Bank of Montreal, $220 million, and PNC, $250 million, according to the filing.</p>
<p>The offer price is expected to be $15.50 per share, according to the filing.</p>
<p>- Beth Harmen, LPC Editorial, 212 489-5455</p>
</text>
